copied, consulted or used as data for this sketch. The upstream package is
UNVERIFIED here.

Method only: the idea of mapping a source request and its translated request
into one shared intermediate record and applying explicit, deterministic
rules (no reference translation, no model call) that separate legitimate
representation changes from information loss, and avoidable loss from
changes forced by target limits. The two toy dialects, the intermediate
record, the 21 rule ids and their definitions, the target profiles, the toy
static target check, the oracle and the fixtures are this sketch's own. No
text, figures, tables or data from the paper are copied into the code; the
PDF was not read; no model was run. The paper's claims appear only in
paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked UNVERIFIED.
